arenafps (working title) credits

Everything in this game is made by its own code:
  - textures (concrete, gravel, grass, paint, steel, wood): procedural PBR sets (albedo, normal, roughness,
    occlusion) generated at load by src/gfx.c, the same generators as the cartwheel demolition derby example
    (MIT, this repository),
  - sounds: synthesised at start from sine and noise in src/fx.c,
  - models: the fighters (skinned, 15 bones, clips idle / run / die), the four first person weapons with gloved
    hands and the arena props (crates, barrels, barriers, columns, planters, pipes, vents, floodlights, consoles)
    are modelled and rigged by our own Blender scripts in tools/blender/ (soldier.py, weapons.py, props.py,
    run with tools/blender/build.sh, headless Blender 5.2) and exported as glTF into models/. Blender itself is
    only the authoring tool (GPL); the exported models are our own work under this game's licence,
  - level geometry (floors, walls, ramps, trim): boxes built in code and merged per material,
  - colour grades: tools/make-luts.mjs writes the three .cube LUTs in luts/,
  - decal sprites (bullet hole, scorch): tools/make-decals.mjs writes textures/*.png,
  - HUD and menus: the engine's shell and its built-in UI font.

Fonts: the engine's built-in UI font; its licence is in the cartwheel-engine NOTICE (open font licence).

Engine libraries: see the cartwheel-engine NOTICE (three.c, Box3D, Recast and Detour (zlib), RVO2 (Apache-2.0),
miniaudio and the rest).

Design references (read for ideas and numbers only; no code, models, textures or sounds were copied):
OpenArena / ioquake3 game code (GPL-2.0, read locally): movement friction and acceleration constants, weapon roles
and spreads, knockback scaling. See internal notes in the engine repository's findings.
